% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §5.4,
% §6.1): trade usage for watches, stated by the authors. The rules for
% which no text was found. A seller names a quartz watch or a mechanical
% watch without saying how it shows the time; the subheadings of an
% electrically operated wrist watch read the display (9102.11 hands, 9102.12
% digits, 9102.19 both). The authors take the usual case:
%   - a quartz wrist watch whose listing names no digital display has hands
%     (a mechanical display);
%   - a watch with a mechanical movement has hands.
% A derived fact says "according to watch trade usage"; the listing and the
% presumed readings leave it out (marketplace.le).
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a thing* is named by the word *a name*.
    *a name* is a word for electrically operated timepieces.
    *a name* is a word for mechanical movements.
    *a name* is a word for opto-electronic displays.
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*.
    *a good* has a mechanical display.

the knowledge base watch trade usage includes these resources:
    watches.

the knowledge base watch trade usage includes:

the authors is published at "https://github.com/LogicalContractsOrg".

rule quartz_watch_has_hands with provenance the authors:
a good has a mechanical display
    if the kind of the good is wrist watch
    and the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for electrically operated timepieces
    and it is not the case that
        the good is named by the word an other name
        and the other name is a word for opto-electronic displays.

rule mechanical_watch_has_hands with provenance the authors:
a good has a mechanical display
    if the good is named by the word a name
    and the name is a word for mechanical movements
    and it is not the case that
        the good is named by the word an other name
        and the other name is a word for opto-electronic displays.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

query displays is:
    which good has a mechanical display.

scenario quartz_and_digital is:
    watch 1 is called "quartz wristwatches".
    watch 2 is called "quartz wristwatches".
    watch 2 is called "digital".
    watch 3 is called "automatic watch".
    displays expects answers ["watch 1 has a mechanical display", "watch 3 has a mechanical display"].
